{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Cannabis Policy to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents relative to cannabis policy matters.","BillNumber":"S2635","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J50","Name":"Joint Committee on Cannabis Policy","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J50","ResponseDate":"2024-02-06T17:02:47.663"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2635/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, February 12, 2024 -- The committee on Cannabis Policy, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 51) of Patricia D. Jehlen for legislation relative to equal opportunity for craft cooperatives; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 55) of Liz Miranda for legislation relative to equitable allocation of cannabis revenue; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 56) of Liz Miranda for legislation relative to the reinvestment of revenues received from the cannabis industry; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 57) of Liz Miranda for legislation to encourage equitable cannabis business ownership; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 60) of Patrick M. O'Connor for legislation to dedicate one-percent of the recreational marijuana excise to youth substance use prevention; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 61) of Patrick M. O'Connor for legislation relative to medical marijuana oversight; and (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1282) of Cynthia Stone Creem (by vote of the town) for legislation to authorize the expenditure of $500,000 from town of Brookline marijuana mitigation stabilization fund for purpose of advancing racial equity in the town of Brookline, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2635).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Cannabis Policy be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 51, 55, 56, 57, 60, 61, and 1282 relative to cannabis policy matters.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J50","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J50"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}